            <ArticleTitle>Painful spondylolisthesis in a two-year-old child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>199-201</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spondylolisthesis is considered one of the common causes of back pain in children. There are far fewer cases reported in children under the age of 4 years. However, all patients described were diagnosed by radiographic examination in a workup for other congenital or musculoskeletal abnormalities. This report describes a 2-year-old girl who presented with low back pain and was subsequently diagnosed with spondylolisthesis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
